{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You are implementing part A of GitHub issue #13 in user/delegate (`gh issue view 13 --comments` for the body and the rulings; spec #4, \"Implementation Decisions\" → \"Surface\" lists what is removed). Do not delegate further: no subagents, no cursor_run, no delegate tools. Follow AGENTS.md.\n\nWorking directory: this worktree, branch `13-contract`. Stay on this branch; do not create branches. Commit when done; do not push.\n\nPART A (this run): remove the MCP server and everything only it used, and remove the dead docs. PART B (renames, setup, plugin, README) is a later run — do not rename anything yet (crate name, env vars, config dir, plugin files, bin/setup.sh, README stay as they are in this run).\n\n1. The supervisor (`src/cli.rs` `supervise`) currently drives one job through `JobRegistry` (src/job_registry.rs): dispatch, on_event, watchdog, heartbeat, finalize, cancel. Replace the registry with a single-job module `src/job.rs` that keeps ONLY what `supervise` uses for its one job (spawn the agent child, event handling, idle/tool-idle watchdog, heartbeat record writes, gate + change-set finalize, cancel). Drop everything multi-job or MCP-only: wait/wait_any/wait_all/poll/block/lookup_answer/mark_superseded/kill_all, the jobs map, path_lock, detach_result, answerable. Move the job_registry tests that exercise kept behaviour (watchdog, heartbeat, cancel, finalize) to the new module; delete the rest.\n2. Delete: src/index.rs, src/index/, src/tool_schemas.rs, src/progress.rs (unless the CLI's progress snapshot needs it — then keep only that), src/validate.rs, src/runner.rs + src/runner/ (move `build_argv` into src/backends/cursor.rs if still needed), src/isolation.rs, src/safety.rs (deny-list check), src/main.rs (the old MCP binary), tests/e2e.rs (MCP e2e). Move `build_deps` (config loading) out of index.rs into src/config.rs. Remove the `cursor-delegate-mcp` default binary target so only `delegate` builds (keep the package name for now).\n3. Delete whatever else becomes dead (`cargo build` + `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` warnings for unused items are your guide): capability modes `plan`/`write-unsandboxed` beyond what the CLI maps, `answer_delegation`, `require_non_claude`, `allow_unsandboxed`, `verify_commands`, `allow_partial_commit` (also reword the dirty-tree concern text so it no longer mentions `allowPartialCommit`), `isolation`, `worktree_name`, `downgraded`, the `family` field and any leftover `family` wording, host-profile fields `promptPreamble`, `verifyCommands`, `requiredDeny`, `deadlineMs`, doctor's plugin-registration and legacy-name checks, MCP progress notifications. Do not delete things the CLI still uses.\n4. Delete docs: spec.md, CODE-REVIEW.md, parity/, docs/superpowers/ (July/August plans and specs), docs/ideas/multi-backend.md. Keep docs/agents/.\n5. Do NOT touch: .github/, tests/fixtures/, scripts/, skills/, .claude-plugin/, bin/setup.sh, README.md, AGENTS.md (part B handles those).\n\nBehaviour must not change for `delegate run|resume|cancel|watch|models|doctor`: tests/cli_e2e.rs, tests/cli_info_e2e.rs and tests/budgets.rs must pass unchanged (you may only adjust imports or delete assertions about removed MCP-only fields — list any such change in your report).\n\nChecks before committing: `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test` all green. Commit with message `refactor: remove the MCP server and its dead code (#13)` ending `Co-Authored-By: Composer 2.5 <noreply@cursor.com>`.\n\nCompletion bar: report the commit SHA, `git diff --stat origin/main` summary line, test counts, and files you deleted, or a failure triage — nothing in between. Then **Friction**: up to 3 bullets on what slowed you, what this brief got wrong or left out, what you'd change (\"none\" is fine). End with a STATUS line.\n\nEnd your final message with a single trailing line that is exactly one of: STATUS: DONE, STATUS: DONE_WITH_CONCERNS, STATUS: BLOCKED, STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT, or STATUS: ERROR. When you need an answer from the orchestrator before you can proceed, put your question in the message body and end with STATUS: NEEDS_CONTEXT."}]},"session_id":"e2d994f1-ef61-48a1-b218-cde928b7cc82"}
